Package: predictVoterIdeologyR
Type: Package
Title: Predict Voter Ideology Using Random Forest Classification Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
        given = "Patrick",
        family = "Mellacher",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "patrick.mellacher@example.com"
    ),
    person(
        given = "Gernot",
        family = "Lechner",
        role = "aut"
    )
    )
Description: Reproduces in R the random forest classification framework
    developed in "Objectifying the Measurement of Voter Ideology With Expert
    Data" (Mellacher and Lechner, 2025). The package provides a pure R
    implementation of exported Python/scikit-learn random forest models and
    achieves high agreement, greater than 98 percent, with the original Python
    implementation. The main function takes a data frame containing six key
    independent variables as input and returns predicted respondent positions
    on three ideology scales: general left-right, economic left-right, and
    GAL-TAN.
